WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:16.412
Unit two: Part 1: Photographs of People. Today you will describe what people are doing and choose the best statement.

4
00:00:16.712 --> 00:00:19.376
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.740
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.619
Photograph.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:29.185
Photograph means a picture taken with a camera.

8
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.179
Look at the photograph.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.064
Your turn. Say: Photograph.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.017
Photograph.

11
00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:39.715
Describe.

12
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.983
Describe means to say what you see.

13
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:45.002
Describe the picture.

14
00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:48.327
Your turn. Say: Describe.

15
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.226
Describe.

16
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.600
Present continuous.

17
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:58.814
Present continuous means the tense for actions happening now.

18
00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:00.360
She is typing.

19
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.811
Your turn. Say: Present continuous.

20
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.260
Present continuous.

21
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:09.925
Gesture.

22
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.508
Gesture means a movement of the body to show meaning.

23
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.652
He is making a gesture.

24
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.554
Your turn. Say: Gesture.

25
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.273
Gesture.

26
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.041
Reach for.

27
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.630
Reach for means to stretch out the hand to take.

28
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.775
She is reaching for a file.

29
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:32.838
Your turn. Say: Reach for.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.945
Reach for.

31
00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:38.487
Hold.

32
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:41.355
Hold means to have in the hands.

33
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.311
He is holding a cup.

34
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:46.000
Your turn. Say: Hold.

35
00:01:48.867 --> 00:01:49.728
Hold.

36
00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:51.542
Distractor.

37
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:55.583
Distractor means a wrong answer that sounds possible.

38
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:57.846
One answer is a distractor.

39
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.940
Your turn. Say: Distractor.

40
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.894
Distractor.

41
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.500
Gather.

42
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:09.284
Gather means to come together.

43
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:11.906
They are gathering around a table.

44
00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:14.902
Your turn. Say: Gather.

45
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:18.582
Gather.

46
00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:22.750
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:25.860
Visal, what happens in Part 1?

48
00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:36.069
You see a photograph and hear four statements. You choose the one that best describes the picture, and the statements are not printed.

49
00:02:37.183 --> 00:02:39.403
What do the correct answers describe?

50
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:50.948
They describe actions happening now, usually with the present continuous, such as a woman is typing at a computer. Look at the people, their actions and the setting.

51
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.759
How do I avoid traps?

52
00:02:54.850 --> 00:03:07.487
Wrong statements may use a word you can see but describe an action that is not happening. For example, they may say the man is buying a cup, when he is only holding it.

53
00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:10.145
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:15.363
Grammar focus: Strategy: look at people, actions and setting.

55
00:03:15.663 --> 00:03:16.792
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.483 --> 00:03:19.529
A woman is typing at a computer.

57
00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:22.753
Some colleagues are gathering around a table.

58
00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:30.497
Before the audio, look at the people, the actions and the setting. Choose the statement that describes exactly what is happening.

59
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.412
Be careful! Don't say: I choose a statement with a seen word.

60
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:40.132
Say: I choose the action that matches.

61
00:03:40.432 --> 00:03:41.689
Match the action.

62
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.210
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.779
A Photograph in the Office.

64
00:03:48.079 --> 00:03:50.543
The photograph shows an office with three people.

65
00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:53.649
One man is holding a cup of coffee.

66
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:57.097
A woman is reaching for a file on a shelf.

67
00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.413
Two colleagues are gathering around a table.

68
00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.002
One statement says the man is buying coffee, but he is only holding it.

69
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.893
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.877
In Part 1 the statements are blank.

71
00:04:13.177 --> 00:04:17.028
A, printed. B, in the question. C, not printed.

72
00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:22.891
The answer is C: not printed.

73
00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.247
Correct answers usually use the blank.

74
00:04:26.547 --> 00:04:31.419
A, present continuous. B, past perfect. C, future perfect.

75
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:37.570
The answer is A: present continuous.

76
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:40.089
What is the man doing?

77
00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:44.693
A, drinking tea. B, holding coffee. C, buying coffee.

78
00:04:48.233 --> 00:04:50.813
The answer is B: holding coffee.

79
00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.635
A distractor may use a word you see but blank.

80
00:04:54.935 --> 00:04:59.435
A, be correct. B, be silent. C, describe a wrong action.

81
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.068
The answer is C: describe a wrong action.

82
00:05:07.217 --> 00:05:08.462
What is the woman doing?

83
00:05:08.762 --> 00:05:12.775
A, reaching for a file. B, typing. C, cooking.

84
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.867
The answer is A: reaching for a file.

85
00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:23.218
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:26.698
How do you answer a Part 1 photograph question?

87
00:05:35.483 --> 00:05:37.158
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:53.650
Before the audio starts, I look at the people, their actions and the setting. I listen for the statement that matches the action exactly. I reject statements that use words from the picture but describe a different action.

89
00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.193
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:57.083 --> 00:06:02.754
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: look at people, actions and setting.

91
00:06:03.054 --> 00:06:06.751
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:06:07.051 --> 00:06:09.309
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:06:09.609 --> 00:06:12.319
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

